ead_tokens":0.0,"cache_write_tokens":0.0,"input_tokens":8081.0,"llm_calls":1,"output_tokens":76.0,"requests":1},"project.portability":{"cache_read_tokens":0.0,"cache_write_tokens":0.0,"input_tokens":1774.4285714285713,"llm_calls":1,"output_tokens":101.28571428571429,"requests":1},"project.symbol-reference-completeness":{"cache_read_tokens":0.0,"cache_write_tokens":0.0,"input_tokens":35993.0,"llm_calls":1,"output_tokens":1782.0,"requests":3}}}},"findings":[{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"Specify how batched-run rendering preserves the landed per-unit code-fragment preservation guarantee (`code_fragments`/`_render_unit`) and define the fallback for an exit-0 preservation failure over a batched document (segment-level verbatim vs. re-render per unit).","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.2889,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Landed `_render_unit` (:378-389) verifies each `code_fragments(text)` survives in-order in pandoc output and returns source verbatim on `preservation_failure` — a load-bearing content-safety invariant (:268-272: 'ANY rewrite … is a content change, not a rendering change').","Plan defines the fallback trigger only as 'a safe-run call's timeout or non-zero exit' and 'segment-level fallback marker'; a pandoc exit-0 output that fails the code-fragment preservation check is neither and is not addressed.","Plan states 'No per-unit re-splitting of a batch's output: the combined wiki is one contiguous segment; reassembly is at the run level' — which removes the per-unit boundary the current preservation check relies on."],"finding":"The batching mechanism does not specify how the landed per-unit code-fragment preservation guarantee (_render_unit / code_fragments, wiki_render.py:376-390, 266-288) is preserved when a maximal run of _RENDER units is rendered as ONE pandoc document, nor the fallback granularity when pandoc exits 0 but silently corrupts a code fragment (a 'preservation_failure' that is neither a timeout nor a non-zero exit).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f89ebf785a3beb677","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach — 'Batch contiguous SAFE units'; Scope — wiki_render.py; AC line 2","norm_id":"n54bf2c24f3398281","priority":0.8889,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","scenarios":["A run of 3 contiguous _RENDER blocks where one contains inline code that pandoc's jira writer escapes; batched render exits 0 but corrupts that fragment — no timeout, no non-zero exit, so no fallback fires and corrupted wiki ships.","A single preservation failure inside a long run degrades the ENTIRE run to verbatim, regressing the landed per-unit fallback granularity (only the one bad unit was previously echoed)."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"State that a batched run's output is still checked against the concatenated `code_fragments` of every _RENDER unit in the run, and that a preservation failure (like a timeout/non-zero exit) degrades that whole run's segment to verbatim Markdown with the segment-level fallback marker — or, if per-unit granularity must be retained, re-render the failed run unit-by-unit before falling back.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8889,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"low","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","l